<p>I got distracted by MojoPad and Kosshi for a while there. Emacs has been plugging away. Always launched. Always handling my writing. It is the centerpiece of my efforts. I have been making changes to it. Nothing too big, but designed to improve my experience in it. I will talk about three of those in this article.</p>
<h2 id="whitespace">Whitespace</h2>
<p>I like seeing the marks for return and tabs. Returns are valid for every file but tabs are valid for only content which is copied from other programs or sources. I like seeing them. I made sure that they show up in Emacs.</p>
<pre><code>(setq whitespace-style '(face          ; Use faces to colorize
                         tabs          ; Look for tabs
                         tab-mark      ; Visualise tabs
                         newline       ; Look for newlines
                         newline-mark))  ; Visualise newlines
;;                         trailing))    ; (Optional) Still show ugly trailing spaces

(setq whitespace-display-mappings
      '(
        ;; Customize the tab marker
        ;; 9 is the ASCII code for Tab. 
        ;; ?\u2192 is the Unicode character '→' (Rightwards Arrow).
        ;; [?\n] is the fallback if the arrow can't be rendered.
        (tab-mark 9 [?\u2192 ?\t] [?\t])

        ;; Customize the newline/return marker
        ;; 10 is the ASCII code for Newline (Line Feed).
        ;; ?\u21b5 is the Unicode character '↵' (Downwards Arrow with Corner Left).
        (newline-mark 10 [?\u21b5 ?\n] [?\n])
        ))</code></pre>
<h2 id="minimal-mode-line">Minimal Mode Line</h2>
<p>I had been using doom modeline and had a elaborate configuration setup for that. See <a href="https://bicycleforyourmind.com/much_ado_about_emacs_001">Much Ado About Emacs 001 - Bicycle For Your Mind</a>.</p>
<p>Decided to make it simpler:</p>
<pre><code>(defun my-modeline-file-path ()
  "Return abbreviated file path if visiting a file."
  (when-let ((file (buffer-file-name)))
    (format " (%s)" (abbreviate-file-name (file-name-directory file)))))

(setq-default mode-line-format
              '("%e"
                "%* "
                my-modeline-buffer-name
                (:eval (my-modeline-file-path)) ;; Displays " (~/projects/app/)"
                mode-line-format-right-align
                "L%l (%p)"
                " "
                my-modeline-major-mode))

(defvar-local my-modeline-buffer-name
  '(:eval
    (when (mode-line-window-selected-p)
      (propertize (format " %s " (buffer-name))))))

(put 'my-modeline-buffer-name 'risky-local-variable t)

(defvar-local my-modeline-major-mode
  '(:eval
    (list
     (propertize "λ" 'face 'shadow)
     " "
     (propertize (capitalize (symbol-name major-mode)) 'face 'bold)))
  "Mode line construct to display the major mode.")

(put 'my-modeline-major-mode 'risky-local-variable t)</code></pre>
<p>Only the information I need, and none of the information I don’t. Looks pretty and minimal too. Added benefit? No external package.</p>
<h2 id="two-spaces-turn-into-a-period-and-space.-next-letter-gets-capitalized.">Two Spaces Turn Into a Period and Space. Next Letter Gets Capitalized.</h2>
<p>I have picked up some bad habits. Two spaces turns into a period, and the next letter is automatically capitalized. macOS lets me do this automatically in some programs. Not Emacs. I needed to rectify that.</p>
<pre><code>;; two spaces to a period
(defun my/double-space-to-period-and-capitalize ()
  "Convert double space to '. ' and capitalize the next typed character."
  (interactive)
  (if (and (eq (char-before) ?\s)
           (not (eq (char-before (1- (point))) ?\s)))
      (progn
        (delete-char -1)
        (insert ". ")
        ;; Read the next key press directly
        (let ((evt (read-event)))
          (if (characterp evt)
              ;; If it's a character, insert its uppercase version
              (insert (upcase (char-to-string evt)))
            ;; If it's a special key (like an arrow key, backspace, etc.), unread it
            (setq unread-command-events (list evt)))))
    (insert " ")))
;; Enable in text-mode (Org, Markdown, Plain text)
(add-hook 'text-mode-hook
          (lambda ()
            (local-set-key (kbd "SPC") #'my/double-space-to-period-and-capitalize)))</code></pre>
